      "writtenOn": "2022-04-13T17:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps I could have been more precise; the issue for this specific comment is that unless set to run on a specific network, the IKE library itself tracks default, and that includes the VPN itself (see [javadoc](http://shortn/_TiLZayogrc)).\n\nSo the solution is to bind it to a specific network (we already do this for the custom-built one [here](http://shortn/_ftpc2kuYY9)). That said, the other cleanup to use registerDefaultNetworkCallback is still worthwhile to reduce the duplicate redefinitions.",
      "parentUuid": "311eabfb_a830e9c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2714,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 2714,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "9a1a3239de4170cedc832ecedc8adda88ca74e77",
